    "body": "Related to #8197.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nRollout prefill only needs the last position's logits to pick the first token. Two prefill call sites in `HybridEngineRollout` called the model without `logits_to_keep`, so the lm_head produced full `[batch, prompt_len, vocab]` logits:\r\n\r\n- `_generate_graph` (graph-capture path)\r\n- `_continuous_prefill_cache`, explicit static-cache branch (models that still expose `_supports_cache_class`)\r\n\r\nThis PR passes `logits_to_keep=1` when the model's `forward` declares the argument, mirroring how Transformers' `generate()` decides. Models without it are unchanged: their `**kwargs` may be forwarded to submodules, so the argument is not passed blindly. The `module.generate()` branch already does this internally and is untouched.\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\r\n- Graph-capture mode: always benefits (prefill calls the model directly).\r\n- Continuous batching: benefits on Transformers versions that still expose `_supports_cache_class` and support `logits_to_keep` (>= 4.50). On Transformers 5.x this path goes through `module.generate()`, which already keeps only the last logits, so behavior is unchanged there.\r\n\r\n## Measurements\r\n\r\nPrefill forward with `StaticCache`. Random-weight Llama with vocab 151936, hidden 1024, 4 layers, bf16. 1× Intel Arc Pro B70.\r\n\r\n| B × T | full logits | `logits_to_keep=1` | peak memory |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 8 × 1024 | 141.7 ms | 43.3 ms | 2.46 → 0.32 GiB |\r\n| 8 × 2048 | 279.0 ms | 79.6 ms | 4.92 → 0.64 GiB |\r\n| 16 × 2048 | 544.7 ms | 149.5 ms | 9.84 → 1.27 GiB |\r\n\r\nThe selected first token is identical in all cases, and it matches the argmax of a plain HF forward. Small models gain the most because the lm_head dominates; for larger models the time saving shrinks, but the full-vocab activation is still avoided.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- New `test_continuous_prefill_requests_last_logits_only`: a model following the Transformers `logits_to_keep` contract gets `logits_to_keep=1` at prefill, and the generated tokens are unchanged. The test fails without the change.\r\n- `tests/unit/runtime/rollout/`: 63 passed, 1 skipped (CPU).\r\n\n\n## Contribution checklist\n\n**Related work.** This relates to #8197 (rollout profiling). A search for `logits_to_keep` and rollout prefill found no other PR.\n\n**Sibling paths checked.** `HybridEngineRollout` has three prefill entry points:\n- graph capture: changed;\n- the explicit static-cache branch of continuous batching: changed;\n- `module.generate()`: already keeps only the last logits, so it is untouched.\n\n**Commands and results.**\n```\npytest -p no:randomly tests/unit/runtime/rollout/\n```\nAt head `fba8f9184`: 63 passed, 1 skipped, both with `DS_ACCELERATOR=cpu` and on 1× Intel Arc Pro B70 (XPU), Level Zero driver 1.15.39122 (compute runtime 26.27.39122.11), torch 2.14.0.dev20260804+xpu, transformers 5.17.0. The measurement table above was taken on the same B70 setup.\n\n**Numerics, performance, memory.** The selected first token is unchanged. Time and peak-memory results are in the Measurements table above.\n\n**Compatibility matrix.**\n\n| | Validated | Not validated |\n|---|---|---|\n| Transformers | 5.17.0 (static-cache prefill on device) | The `_supports_cache_class` branch on <5.x is covered only by the unit test |\n| Rollout path | Prefill forward on device; continuous prefill in the unit test | End-to-end graph-capture rollout on device |\n| ZeRO | | Hybrid engine with ZeRO-3 |\n| Precision | bf16 | fp16 |\n| Accelerator | XPU, CPU | CUDA |\n\n**AI assistance.** This PR was developed with AI assistance (GitHub Copilot CLI). I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n",
